Subject: [PATCH 02108/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1 (THE
 HEADLINE; P0 oracle-distinct frontier) -- CLOSE the cross-GENERATOR axis with
 a NON-degenerate ARC-GEN pool. .395 proved the oracle-distinct
 verifier-beats-vote win generalizes across families CARVED FROM ONE POOL
 (exp4271 +0.40 held-out, leak-free, 5-seed). The .396 ARC-GEN 2nd-substrate
 attempt (exp4282) was FLAGGED DEGENERATE: the pool was wrong-majority-only
 (vote@1=0.0 structural) with 4 candidates/task (correct trivially separable
 -> set_encoder@1=1.0), giving a meaningless +1.0 CI[1.0,1.0] that measures
 pool degeneracy, NOT cross-generator transfer (audit:
 docs/research-notes/exp4282-arcgen-degenerate-audit-2026-06-16.md). The
 cross-GENERATOR axis -- whether the verifier transfers to a
 CONSTRUCTION-DISJOINT generator -- is the LAST open axis of the selection
 moat. REBUILD a NON-degenerate ARC-GEN pool (arXiv:2511.00162,
 github.com/google/ARC-GEN; gitignore the clone): realistic candidate counts
 (NOT wrong-majority-only -- include tasks where vote CAN win), report vote@1
 well above 0 and an oracle ceiling BELOW 1.0 (headroom the verifier must
 EARN). Train the set-encoder on train-generators; test beats-vote on HELD-OUT
 generators. Report per-substrate lift SEPARATELY (original-ARC / ARC-TGI /
 ARC-GEN). Emit cross_generator_holds BARE bool := (held-out ARC-GEN delta>0
 AND CI95-excl-0 AND vote_at_1>0.05 AND oracle_at_k<1.0 AND delta<0.95 -- the
 non-degenerate guards). verifier_is_oracle=false. HARD-CAP to the window; an
 honest partial pool (>=5 generators, >=~12 held-out tasks/fold) is fine.

